      "description": "Watch Cambridge United vs Wigan Athletic highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. The League One fixture on August 15, 2026, delivered a captivating spectacle of football as Cambridge United and Wigan Athletic faced off in a match defined by dramatic shifts in momentum. Supporters at the ground witnessed a contest that evolved from total dominance to a frantic, nail-biting conclusion. Cambridge Take Control Early Cambridge United wasted no time in establishing their presence, surging into the lead after just three minutes. Kelland Watts found the net following a well-placed delivery from Mamadou Jobe , setting a high-tempo tone for the opening stages. The home side continued to exploit gaps in the Wigan Athletic defense, and their persistence was rewarded again in the 34th minute. Louis Appere clinical finish doubled the advantage, ensuring Cambridge headed into the break with a commanding two-goal cushion. A Tale of Two Halves The momentum showed no signs of slowing down early in the second half when Isaac Heath extended the lead to 3-0 in the 53rd minute. At that stage, the result seemed a formality, but Wigan Athletic staged a remarkable recovery that silenced the home crowd. The fightback began in the 69th minute through Sonny Perkins , who sparked life back into the visitors. Just four minutes later, substitute Akeel Higgins converted an assist from Dara Costelloe to make it 3-2, setting the stage for a dramatic final twenty minutes. Defensive Grit and the Final Whistle As the clock ticked down, the atmosphere grew increasingly tense. Wigan Athletic pushed forward in search of a late equalizer, forcing Cambridge into a defensive shell. Tactical changes saw Patrick Bauer introduced to shore up the backline, while Wigan brought on Callum McManaman to add creative flair. In the dying moments of stoppage time, Zak Bradshaw received a yellow card as the physical battle intensified. Despite the late pressure, Cambridge United held onto their 3-2 lead until the final whistle, securing a hard-fought victory in a thriller that will be remembered for its emotional swings."
